-# The editor's notice slot for what the last submission did, above the form.
-# Three states: nothing to say, a refused Save, or a repair that changed the text
-# without storing it. What the buffer itself holds is a separate slot below this
-# one — see xml/_escape_advisory.
-#
-# locals: errors (Array) — the validation messages from a refused Save; empty
-# when the last Save was not refused. repairable (Boolean) — whether one of those
-# messages is about a control character, which the editor can fix on request.
-# repaired (Symbol, nil) — which repair just rewrote the editor's text, so the
-# confirmation names the change the curator asked for and can read in the buffer.
-#
-# The container renders whatever the state, because both the Validate and the
-# Repair turbo_streams replace this node — Turbo needs the target to be on the
-# page to find it, and the id has to survive each replacement.
#save_refusal
  - if errors.present?
    .alert.alert-danger{role: "alert"}
      %h5.alert-heading Not saved — this XML is not valid
      %p.mb-2 Your changes are still in the editor below. Correct the problem and save again.
      %ul.mb-0
        - errors.each do |err|
          %li= err.to_s
      - if repairable
        = render 'repair_offer', kind: 'control_characters',
                                 label: 'Replace the control characters',
                                 variant: 'danger'
  - elsif repaired == :control_characters
    .alert.alert-warning{role: "alert"}
      %h5.alert-heading Control characters replaced — nothing saved yet
      %p.mb-0
        Each one became a line break, so the words either side of it stay apart.
        Read the editor below, then Validate + Preview or Save.
  - elsif repaired == :double_escapes
    .alert.alert-warning{role: "alert"}
      %h5.alert-heading Double escapes decoded — nothing saved yet
      %p.mb-0
        Each one became the character it spelled out, one level only.
        Read the editor below, then Validate + Preview or Save.
